senses
  entry
    definition "no longer in your possession or control; unable to be found or recovered"
    examples ("a lost child" "lost friends" "his lost book" "lost opportunities")
    id oewn-01452455-a
    partOfSpeech a
  entry
    definition "spiritually or physically doomed or destroyed"
    examples ("lost souls" "a lost generation" "a lost ship" "the lost platoon")
    id oewn-01453748-a
    partOfSpeech a
  entry
    definition "not gained or won"
    examples ("a lost battle" "a lost prize")
    id oewn-01455045-a
    partOfSpeech a
  entry
    definition "people who are destined to die soon"
    examples ("the agony of the doomed was in his voice")
    id oewn-07963280-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (doomed)
  entry
    definition "having lost your bearings; confused as to time or place or personal identity"
    examples ("I frequently find myself disoriented when I come up out of the subway" "the anesthetic left her completely disoriented")
    id oewn-01688793-s
    partOfSpeech s
    synonyms (confused disoriented)
  entry
    definition "cannot be recovered or regained"
    examples ("his lost honor")
    id oewn-01963677-s
    partOfSpeech s
  entry
    definition "not caught with the senses or the mind"
    examples ("words lost in the din")
    id oewn-00537393-s
    partOfSpeech s
    synonyms (missed)
  entry
    definition "deeply absorbed in thought"
    examples ("as distant and bemused as a professor listening to the prattling of his freshman class" "lost in thought" "a preoccupied frown")
    id oewn-02427955-s
    partOfSpeech s
    synonyms (bemused preoccupied)
  entry
    definition "perplexed by many conflicting situations or statements; filled with bewilderment"
    examples ("obviously bemused by his questions" "bewildered and confused" "a cloudy and confounded philosopher" "just a mixed-up kid" "she felt lost on the first day of school")
    id oewn-01770645-s
    partOfSpeech s
    synonyms (baffled befuddled bemused bewildered confounded confused mazed mixed-up "at sea")
  entry
    definition "unable to function; without help"
    id oewn-01233489-s
    partOfSpeech s
    synonyms (helpless)
  entry
    definition "fail to keep or to maintain; cease to have, either physically or in an abstract sense"
    examples ("She lost her purse when she left it unattended on her seat")
    id oewn-02292634-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "fail to win"
    examples ("We lost the battle but we won the war")
    id oewn-01102003-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "suffer the loss of a person through death or removal"
    examples ("She lost her husband in the war" "The couple that wanted to adopt the child lost her when the biological parents claimed her")
    id oewn-01799093-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "miss from one's possessions; lose sight of"
    examples ("I've lost my glasses again!")
    id oewn-02292463-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "allow to go out of sight or mind"
    examples ("The detective lost the man he was shadowing after he had to stop at a red light" "lose the crowds by climbing a mountain" "the lost tribe")
    id oewn-02201537-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "fail to make money in a business; make a loss or fail to profit"
    examples ("I lost thousands of dollars on that bad investment!" "The company turned a loss after the first year")
    id oewn-02293733-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose "turn a loss")
  entry
    definition "fail to get or obtain"
    examples ("I lost the opportunity to spend a year abroad")
    id oewn-02293000-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "fail to perceive or to catch with the senses or the mind"
    examples ("I missed that remark" "She missed his point" "We lost part of what he said")
    id oewn-02132318-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (miss lose)
  entry
    definition "withdraw, as from reality"
    examples ("he lost himself in his music")
    id oewn-00497220-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (lose)
  entry
    definition "be set at a disadvantage"
    examples ("This author really suffers in translation" "The painting loses something in this light")
    id oewn-00205234-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (suffer lose)
